questions.explanation:
NCERT lists several roles of transpiration:
- it creates transpiration pull for absorption and transport;
- it supplies water for photosynthesis;
- it carries minerals from soil to all parts;
- it maintains shape through turgidity.
It also cools leaf surfaces, sometimes by 10 to 15 °C, through evaporative cooling.
1 to 2 °C is too small. 30 °C or more is unrealistic.
Answer: (2)
